Read or update the active PCB's design rules through typed EDA actions.
Preserves unspecified settings. Values default to mil; --unit mm converts to
the rule's storage unit. Every write supports --dry-run and readback.
This changes rules, not existing tracks/vias or global editor preferences.
Use --project and --doc to select the target. Save, reload and read back to
verify persistence. See pcb stackup/origin and silk-add/silk-set for other
exam settings. Grid/snap/global preferences are currently unsupported.

Usage:
  easyeda pcb config [flags]
  easyeda pcb config [command]

Examples:
  easyeda pcb config get --project ceshi
  easyeda pcb config track --name copperThickness1oz --min 8 --default 8 --dry-run --project ceshi --doc PCB1

Available Commands:
  bind        Assign a track rule to an existing net class and every member
  clearance   Set only Track-to-Track clearance across existing layer tables
  get         Export current rules, net classes and assignments
  net-color   Set one network's RGB color, preserving transparency
  track       Set track width limits, or copy an existing rule into a new named rule
  via         Set via outer/hole diameter limits without changing existing vias

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for config

Global Flags:
      --doc string                pin every mutating action to this schematic page / PCB (uuid or name): the CLI switches to it and confirms via live document.current before editing, refusing rather than land the edit on whatever page is foreground — removes the doc-switch race
      --force-stale-read string   deprecated compatibility option; stale PCB reads now continue with staleRisk and authoritative workflows still save, reload, then read back
      --host string               daemon host (default "127.0.0.1")
      --ports string              daemon port range (start-end) (default "60832-60841")
      --project string            route by project name/uuid instead of --window (survives windowId churn)
      --skip-version-check        deprecated compatibility option; version differences are diagnostic and no longer block actions
      --window string             EasyEDA window ID

Use "easyeda pcb config [command] --help" for more information about a command.
